    "body": "<!-- pr-reviewer: 863fae5ba738d1426e0d47d4ef6c5553cc19decc -->\nNot built - needs a maintainer look at `.github/workflows/release.yml`.\n\nNo blocking findings from the source review.\n\nWhat looks good:\n- The checksum patterns match the published package patterns.\n- The step runs in `dist/`, so the checksum file contains basenames.\n- The step refuses an empty asset set and verifies the checksum file before publication.\n- The checksum file excludes itself and `release-body.md`.\n- The workflow triggers, permissions, and job dependencies do not change.\n\nLocal review results:\n- Trial merge with upstream main `b44a422bbc5b56d6c12f5a1adcb693fbf44c2692`: clean.\n- Trial merge `7219b0f3d5050945c5965cd4e1282d3e3b389867`: its first parent is the reviewed PR head.\n- `git diff upstream/main HEAD --check`: passed.\n- Build, quick gate, heavy lanes, and clippy: not run. The reviewer rules require source review without execution for `.github/` changes.\n- The author reports passing checks in the PR body. I did not repeat those checks.\n- No GitHub runner or release workflow was started.\n\nExtra suites run:\n- None. The diff changes no fixture, importer, kernel, or UI files.\n\nSafety and mutations:\n- The diff changes no posted G-code, geometry, collision checks, gouge checks, or stock simulation.\n- Mutations: not applicable. No golden files change.\n\nRequested before merge: none from the source review. The maintainer must decide whether to accept the workflow change.\n\nNotes:\n- PR #3110 proposes the same checksum publication. Select one implementation before merge.\n- `Refs #2428` correctly identifies this as partial work. The update feature remains outside this PR.\n- Live release execution and artifact upload remain unverified.\n- The review worktree and branch remain in place for the next review round.\n\nLabel: `needs-maintainer`. The PR is mergeable, but the workflow change has not been executed by this reviewer.\n\nA maintainer will approve and merge by hand.\n",
